A. validating the divergence-theorem estimator against two exact answers
====================================================================================================================
  A1 sphere identity for a point mass: at r = 500 kpc, y = 0.5958, so M_ph must be exactly nu_tilde(y) M = 8.5923e+13 Msun
  A2 deep-MOND cylinder, point mass 1e+14 Msun, R = 300 kpc, |z| < 18 Mpc:
       analytic  sqrt(M a0/G) * int arctan(Z/rho) drho = 1.21454e+14 Msun
       quadrature                                      = 1.20759e+14 Msun   (error -0.572%)
  [PASS] 57-A the surface-integral estimator reproduces the exact deep-MOND cylinder mass of a point source to better than a percent, so the projected phantom masses below are quadrature-limited and not resolution-limited   (quadrature 1.2076e+14 vs analytic 1.2145e+14, error -0.572%)
  [PASS] M1 mutation: with nu_tilde = 0 (no modification at all) the estimator returns exactly zero phantom mass, so nothing in the quadrature is manufacturing mass by itself   (nu_tilde = 0 gives M_ph = -0.000e+00 Msun against a signal of 1.215e+14)

====================================================================================================================
B. the published baryon model, checked against the paper it comes from
====================================================================================================================
  total baryonic mass of the model = 2.392e+14 Msun (the paper quotes ~2.4e14)
  projected baryons within 300 kpc: BCG1 4.203e+13 Msun (paper: ~4.6e13), BCG3 2.359e+13 Msun (paper: ~2.45e13)
  [PASS] 57-B the Plummer model transcribed here reproduces the published projected baryonic masses at both galaxy peaks, so the model is the one the paper used and not a garbled copy of it   (BCG1 4.203e+13 vs 4.6e13 (-8.6%), BCG3 2.359e+13 vs 2.45e13 (-3.7%))
  note the offsets that make this cluster what it is: the main GAS clump sits at (190, 90) kpc while the main
  GALAXIES sit at (0, 0); the subcluster gas at (670, 170) while its galaxies are at (820, 220) -- 158 kpc apart.

